Nivel de vechime: Nivel mediu de experiență
Tip de angajare: Full-time
Sectoare de activitate: Servicii IT și consultanță IT
The role of the HQ professionals is to provide expertise, advice, selection and implementation of customized IT solutions for client companies and to maintain the information framework at a high level of functionality, accessibility and performance.
 The responsibilities of the System Administrator include but are not limited to:
Install and configure desktop and server systems including hardware, OS and applications;
Implement and troubleshoot network infrastructures;
Configure, monitor and troubleshot windows / linux server systems;
IT infrastructure administration for client companies;
Remote or on-site client support ;
Hardware and software diagnostics and resolution for servers, desktops, notebooks, networking and peripheral equipment;
Address incidents, monitor ticket queue, and coordinate with others in service support team;
Communicate effectively with customers and peers.
 We are looking for:
A result-oriented person, adaptable to various situations and tasks, able to identify problems and to apply the best solutions;
A self-driven individual who takes initiative and thrives in a dynamic and fast-paced environment;
Dedication to learning and staying current with industry trends, technologies, and best practices;
A genuine passion for the IT field and a desire to continually evolve and grow professionally;
A minimum of 1-2 year experience, solid IT background or certifications in the field;
Good knowledge in networking and PC management;
Understanding of TCP/IP, DNS, DHCP, VLANs, and routing principles to configure and troubleshoot network devices and connectivity issues;
Good knowledge and/or experience with backup and replication software;
Good knowledge and/or experience with both Windows and Linux server environments;
Good knowledge and/or experience in email servers administration;
Knowledge of virtualization platforms such as VMware vSphere, Microsoft Hyper-V or Proxmox, including the ability to deploy, manage, and troubleshoot virtual machines;
Experience in applying security patches and updates to servers and workstations in a controlled and timely manner;
Awareness of security tools and best practices, including firewalls, intrusion detection systems (IDS), antivirus software, and security protocols;
Good knowledge and/or experience with Microsoft 365 administration is a plus;
Good knowledge and/or experience with Microsoft Azure is a plus;
Experience with disaster recovery strategies to ensure data integrity and business continuity is a plus;
Familiar with hardware/software/networking diagnostic and monitoring tools;
 We are offering:
Professional, friendly work environment;
Training and career development opportunities;
Work schedule flexibility from the office/home;
Complete medical services pack;
Salary range between 1000 and 1700 euro net/month.
